      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T09:12:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, after looking through the code I found that there is also a dependency from the `AutoReindexScheduler` to `ChangeReindexRunnable` to `ForwardedIndexChangeHandler` where the `ChangeReindexRunnable` passes `Optional.empty()` when calling `ForwardedIndexChangeHandler.index(...)`. In that case we do not have an `IndexEvent` to pass. So we either have to build it at the calling place (by taking the current sha1\u0027s of the change metaref and target branch) or we have to continue supporting `Optional\u003cIndexEvent\u003e`. Note that whichever solution we decide to accept, we shall make both sha1\u0027s in the IndexEvent mandatory. There is no point in keeping both `Optional\u003cIndexEvent\u003e` as the parameter type and then also allowing some fields in the `IndexEvent` to be optional (null).",
      "parentUuid": "a5a6aef2_e56991d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "9986134abc33e5bb3a73c3c2d11808b354d09096",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5ba7d45_6f4f5181",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
